We are presenting several papers at BPM 2026 in Toronto: “Characterizing Process Variants with Natural Examples” (Main Conference), “Visual Comparative Analysis of Process Variants Data” and “From Event Logs to Process Performance Indicators via Declarative Process Mining” (BPM Forum), and “Simulating the Domain Expert: An Empirical Evaluation of LLM-Based Interview Training for Business Process Modeling” (BPM Educators Forum). I also co-organized the “Workshop on Forgotten, Overlooked, and Rejected Topics in Business Process Management” (FOR-BPM) with Iris Beerepoot and Tijs Slaats.
